<div class="alert alert-info">
  The autocomplete endpoint must return a JSON array in the format <code>[{ value: 'CH', label: 'Switzerland' }, ...]</code>.<br>
  The <code>value</code> key is used to fill the input field and the <code>label</code> key is used to display the results.
</div>
<div class="mb-3"
     data-controller="autocomplete"
     data-autocomplete-url-value="<%= main_app.countries_path %>">
  <label for="example-autocomplete" class="form-label">Country</label>
  <input class="form-control"
         id="example-autocomplete"
         placeholder="Start typing a country name"
         data-autocomplete-target="input">
</div>

<hr>

<div class="alert alert-info">
  You can decide which attribute is used to display the values and which one is used to fill the input field.
</div>

<div class="mb-3"
     data-controller="autocomplete"
     data-autocomplete-url-value="<%= main_app.countries_path %>"
     data-autocomplete-input-param-value="label">
  <label for="example-autocomplete" class="form-label">Country</label>
  <input class="form-control"
         id="example-autocomplete"
         placeholder="Start typing a country name"
         data-autocomplete-target="input">
</div>

<hr>

<div class="alert alert-info">
  You can also have a separate field for the value. Usually hidden.
</div>

<div class="row mb-3"
     data-controller="autocomplete"
     data-autocomplete-url-value="<%= main_app.countries_path %>">
  <div class="col-6">
  <label for="example-autocomplete" class="form-label">Country name</label>
  <input class="form-control"
         id="example-autocomplete"
         placeholder="Start typing a country name"
         data-autocomplete-target="input">
  </div>
  <div class="col-6">
  <label for="hidden-autocomplete" class="form-label">Country ISO</label>
  <input class="form-control"
         id="hidden-autocomplete"
         placeholder="This field would probably be hidden"
         data-autocomplete-target="hidden">
  </div>
</div>

<hr>

<div class="alert alert-info">
  We took inspiration and code from
  <a href="https://github.com/afcapel/stimulus-autocomplete" target="_blank">afcapel/stimulus-autocomplete</a>
  to create this component.
</div>
